daemon: Bridge short contact dropouts (LiftGraceMs)

[Touchpad] LiftGraceMs: a valid contact that vanishes for less than this
many milliseconds and reappears within 5 mm of its last position is treated
as continuous. No lift and no touch down are emitted, the tracking id stays
the same, and the button motion gating does not see a contact appear or
disappear. Bridges sensor detection dropouts, which cause ghost taps while
sliding and ghost right clicks while two-finger scrolling.

Held contacts are released by time, not by frames: the runner waits for data
with poll() (hid::Device::wait) while a contact is held and calls
Application::on_timeout() when the grace time runs out, so a sensor that stops
streaming after the last finger lifts cannot leave a stuck touch.

The idea comes from the comment on LiftGraceMs in ProgrammerIn-wonderland's
ELLX iptsd build (https://public.hgci.org/software/ELLX/iptsd/); that code
is not published, this is an independent implementation.

